-Spain- FC Cataluña's Practice Field {Typesetting:  I'd like this to be: "Spain - Practice Field of FC Cataluna" (with the accent over the "n", of course) in order to remain consistent with the previous ep.}

01:59.740 --> 02:01.260
The coach is here!

02:01.710 --> 02:02.900
Let's hurry!

02:02.900 --> 02:03.700
Coach!

02:06.780 --> 02:08.920
Good morning, Coach.

02:08.920 --> 02:11.150
Yes, good morning.

02:11.150 --> 02:14.820
Coach, Tsubasa was taken to the infirmary yesterday.

02:14.820 --> 02:17.820
Was that Rivaul giving him a baptism by fire?

02:17.820 --> 02:20.820
Was his greeting that severe?

02:21.450 --> 02:26.980
Does this mean that King Rivaul already recognizes Tsubasa's talents?

02:26.980 --> 02:31.820
If that's the case, doesn't that increase your belief in Tsubasa?

02:32.440 --> 02:36.750
Is Tsubasa one of the candidates being considered as a regular starting member?

02:36.750 --> 02:38.340
What do you think about him?

02:40.660 --> 02:45.190
It's normal that you Japanese journalists expect a lot from Tsubasa,

02:45.190 --> 02:48.880
but this training camp is just starting.

02:48.880 --> 02:51.820
I haven't finished making my plans for the upcoming season yet.

02:57.190 --> 03:02.380
Those who don't produce results during the camp won't be part of those plans.

03:09.470 --> 03:14.620
<b>Run to the Opening Match!</b>

03:09.470 --> 03:14.620
<b>Run to the Opening Match!</b>

03:16.090 --> 03:20.100
We'll now be having a game between the regulars and the substitutes.

03:20.570 --> 03:21.670
Huh?

03:21.670 --> 03:24.330
A practice game already? On the second day?

03:24.330 --> 03:26.670
And they're doing it like a real game?

03:26.670 --> 03:27.860
Wow!

03:28.350 --> 03:32.910
Marono, Sylvio, Tomas, Felíz, Carbona!

03:32.910 --> 03:35.380
You five will be going to the substitutes' field.

03:39.720 --> 03:42.180
Regular players, put on your yellow shirts!

03:42.180 --> 03:46.140
So he's telling those guys that they need more training?

03:46.140 --> 03:48.310
That's harsh.

03:49.630 --> 03:52.460
Will Tsubasa be playing in this game?

03:53.190 --> 03:55.900
Rivaul is obviously on the regulars' side.

03:55.900 --> 04:00.500
Clemente and Almieja, who are back from injuries, are also playing as regulars?

04:00.920 --> 04:02.680
Next up, the subs' side!

04:02.680 --> 04:03.700
Hold on a bit.

04:03.700 --> 04:04.620
All right.

04:05.590 --> 04:09.260
Gonzales-san is a sub and not a regular?

04:10.750 --> 04:16.790
Listen, the fight to become a starting member for the opening game is already beginning.

04:16.790 --> 04:20.650
If you want to play games, show them what you've got.

04:24.140 --> 04:25.000
Yeah.

04:26.260 --> 04:27.900
Tsubasa!

04:28.410 --> 04:32.130
You'll be the playmaker for the subs' side.

04:32.700 --> 04:33.940
Yes!

04:33.940 --> 04:37.460
Awesome, Tsubasa's getting to play!

04:37.460 --> 04:40.330
Tsubasa is the playmaker!

04:40.330 --> 04:41.510
Yes!

04:44.830 --> 04:48.000
He's already putting Tsubasa against Rivaul?

04:48.000 --> 04:52.030
Is this Coach Edward's way of testing Tsubasa?

04:58.580 --> 05:04.640
Tsubasa, this practice game is a chance for the subs to become starters,

05:04.640 --> 05:08.210
but the regulars will not be letting up an inch

05:08.210 --> 05:11.020
because if they do, they'll be demoted to being subs.

05:11.630 --> 05:15.340
Edward is setting high standards even at practice.

05:15.340 --> 05:16.540
Keep that in mind!

05:17.130 --> 05:18.540
Yeah.

05:27.220 --> 05:28.640
Rivaul-san.

05:32.090 --> 05:34.950
Tsubasa's playing the practice game?

05:34.950 --> 05:37.500
Looks like it'll be interesting!

05:41.790 --> 05:46.740
Albert is keeping the ball just as well as he does with his Dutch national team.

05:49.110 --> 05:50.490
Tsubasa's on his way!

05:52.540 --> 05:53.620
Here comes trouble.

05:54.450 --> 05:55.620
Albert!

05:56.130 --> 05:56.900
He's going to pass!

05:59.570 --> 06:01.210
Tsubasa is cutting into the pass path!

06:07.800 --> 06:08.940
Damn it!

06:08.940 --> 06:09.950
Close!

06:15.940 --> 06:17.870
Go for it, Gonzales!

06:17.870 --> 06:20.300
Don't hold back against Rivaul!

06:21.150 --> 06:22.300
Here I come!

06:25.370 --> 06:27.660
Bernhardt is coming up the side.

06:27.660 --> 06:29.450
Is Rivaul going to pass or dribble through?

06:52.400 --> 06:54.980
He's already coming out with his "Rivaul Turn"?

06:54.980 --> 06:57.280
I-Incredible!

06:57.280 --> 06:59.140
Is that the Rivaul Turn?

07:01.890 --> 07:04.580
Rivaul's going straight for the goal while dribbling.

07:11.930 --> 07:16.590
That's the feint that's said to be among the best in the world?

07:24.720 --> 07:26.570
Are you a Japanese journalist?

07:26.570 --> 07:29.580
Eh? Well, something like that.

07:29.580 --> 07:33.520
I'm Mendez, the team doctor.

07:33.520 --> 07:37.900
How do you think Tsubasa Ohzora is doing here in Cataluña?

07:40.420 --> 07:46.270
He's in the best environment possible for closely studying the moves of very good players.

07:46.270 --> 07:50.740
Oh? The idea of Rivaul putting him out of commission doesn't frighten you? 

07:50.740 --> 07:56.830
No, this generation of Japanese players are always aiming for the top.

07:56.830 --> 07:59.900
And Tsubasa's one of them.

08:02.220 --> 08:04.820
His generation's always aiming for the top?

08:17.580 --> 08:20.460
Clemente's doing his "Snake Mark"!

08:20.460 --> 08:23.300
I'm finally back from injury!

08:23.300 --> 08:27.500
I'll stand out during this practice game, so I can get back my starting position!

08:38.460 --> 08:40.160
Incredible!

08:40.160 --> 08:43.570
He cleared Clemente using only his upper body!

08:48.810 --> 08:50.820
W-Who is this guy?

08:52.880 --> 08:57.500
Back then, he was splendidly keeping his balance,

08:57.500 --> 09:01.420
but this time, he cleared my marking in an instant!

09:05.380 --> 09:10.570
He built up his body to this extent after training for such a short time?

09:14.050 --> 09:16.460
I'll be taking on that big wall!{there's no rule that says we can't use both "wall" or "obstacle"}

09:16.460 --> 09:17.620
Let's get to it!

09:20.670 --> 09:23.970
Tsubasa, this will be the end of your showing off!

09:29.470 --> 09:30.860
Tsubasa, behind you!

09:30.860 --> 09:32.020
Gonzales-san!

09:37.100 --> 09:38.900
What? A heel pass?

09:43.310 --> 09:47.580
He's rushing straight at Rivaul without paying attention to Albert and Putini.

09:48.590 --> 09:51.440
Does he want to challenge Rivaul that badly?

09:51.440 --> 09:58.100
Are you really thinking you can beat Rivaul and steal his position as the playmaker?

09:58.600 --> 10:01.620
Interesting. I want to see that challenge!

10:02.220 --> 10:04.100
Here you go, Tsubasa!

10:07.460 --> 10:10.180
Gonzales made a loop pass?

10:10.180 --> 10:12.420
Thank you, Gonzales-san!

10:14.030 --> 10:17.150
Rivaul is rushing towards Gonzales' pass!

10:23.960 --> 10:26.140
I can't wait for the ball to drop!

10:26.140 --> 10:27.420
All right.

10:29.640 --> 10:32.460
I'll just get the ball first!

11:20.850 --> 11:23.340
Rivaul's better than Tsubasa in mid-air.

11:32.420 --> 11:34.620
Tsubasa's got the ball?

11:39.410 --> 11:42.110
He stole the ball from Rivaul?

11:42.110 --> 11:46.260
He even managed to keep it during that collision?

11:53.060 --> 11:54.650
Let's do this!

11:56.530 --> 11:58.260
What a guy!

11:58.260 --> 12:00.330
He's still going for Rivaul!

12:14.220 --> 12:15.660
T-That was...

12:16.370 --> 12:20.070
Tsubasa did a Rivaul Turn?!

12:20.070 --> 12:21.810
That's like him.

12:22.920 --> 12:27.900
He absorbs all the best moves of his opponents.

12:36.200 --> 12:40.660
He's using it! He's using his "High-speed Submarine Defense" at ground level!

12:47.910 --> 12:48.930
No way!

12:49.640 --> 12:51.630
Tsubasa avoided it!

12:52.970 --> 12:54.700
How about this?

12:57.480 --> 13:01.460
No way! Rivaul took the ball from Tsubasa in his air space!

13:17.700 --> 13:20.940
I can't surpass him even though I'm giving my all.

13:20.940 --> 13:26.150
Rivaul-san uses techniques that involve both the upper and lower parts of his body.

13:26.150 --> 13:29.300
These are, indeed, the best techniques from the best player in the world.

13:29.300 --> 13:36.290
Is Tsubasa a mere chick compared to the Falcon of Cataluña?

13:36.290 --> 13:40.380
But it's the first time we've seen a new player like him!

13:41.250 --> 13:46.290
He challenged Rivaul right from the start,

13:46.290 --> 13:49.810
and is even making him play seriously.

13:49.810 --> 13:50.660
True.

13:51.380 --> 13:54.380
Nicely fought, Tsubasa!

13:54.730 --> 13:57.620
No matter how many times you fall, keep gunning for him!

13:57.620 --> 13:59.300
I'm with you!

14:01.130 --> 14:02.300
Doc...

14:02.680 --> 14:03.380
Tsubasa!

14:08.940 --> 14:11.260
Y-Yes!

14:17.360 --> 14:19.260
What's your goal?

14:20.940 --> 14:22.260
My goal?

14:56.310 --> 14:57.780
My dream is...

14:58.520 --> 15:02.530
to become the best player in the world.

15:02.530 --> 15:04.540
That's why I came here.

15:07.950 --> 15:10.540
If that's the case, follow me no matter what happens!

15:12.060 --> 15:17.770
By doing that, you'll become a lot better and a lot stronger!

15:19.190 --> 15:20.100
Yes!

15:21.310 --> 15:22.200
Let's do it!

15:22.200 --> 15:23.110
Yes!

15:26.930 --> 15:30.790
Was that Rivaul accepting Tsubasa?

15:30.790 --> 15:32.310
I-I guess so...

15:32.850 --> 15:34.730
The game has resumed!

15:34.730 --> 15:37.810
I'll be sure to succeed!

15:37.810 --> 15:42.040
The obstacle to pass is so close to me!

15:59.790 --> 16:01.450
All right, time for a break!

16:06.640 --> 16:07.660
Katagiri-san!

16:08.480 --> 16:10.180
You came here, didn't you?

16:10.180 --> 16:15.350
Yes. I wanted to see how you players are doing abroad.

16:15.350 --> 16:16.660
I see.

16:16.660 --> 16:23.180
I've been having great fun watching you challenge the summits, as always.

16:23.180 --> 16:26.540
I'm learning a lot from Rivaul-san.

16:26.540 --> 16:31.070
I'm also getting prepared to face my next objective.

16:31.070 --> 16:34.040
You guys will change Japanese soccer.

16:34.920 --> 16:35.660
I'm counting on you.

16:35.660 --> 16:36.910
Right.

16:37.730 --> 16:40.170
Tsubasa, we're resuming!

16:44.050 --> 16:48.780
Katagiri-san, please give my regards to everybody.

16:49.230 --> 16:55.310
From here on, Tsubasa will be able to show the talent you talked about.

16:55.310 --> 16:56.030
Yes.

16:57.560 --> 17:02.500
You all will be doing that on the stage we're all aiming for:

17:03.880 --> 17:09.540
the International Cup, the grandest stage that's waiting for you.

17:10.660 --> 17:15.420
Germany - Roland Stadium

17:11.150 --> 17:18.210
This is the opening game of the German League between FC Roland and FC Grunwald.

17:18.210 --> 17:22.890
The first half finished with 0-0, and we're now starting the second half.

17:22.890 --> 17:25.540
FC Roland is the home team.

17:25.540 --> 17:29.630
They want to beat the powerful FC Grunwald to build up some momentum,

17:29.630 --> 17:31.540
but time's running out.

17:31.540 --> 17:35.790
Franz Schester, Roland's lead player, is attacking FC Grunwald.

17:35.790 --> 17:37.880
He's now passing the center of the field!

17:39.410 --> 17:43.610
Schester has, at his left side, his tall forward, Manfred Margas,

17:43.610 --> 17:49.360
and to his right, Ramon Victorino, a player from Uruguay's national team who just joined the team.

17:49.360 --> 17:54.040
This "Young Triangle" is challenging FC Grunwald!

17:59.740 --> 18:01.100
Go!

18:01.100 --> 18:03.460
Schester kicks a powerful pass!

18:04.190 --> 18:07.060
It speeds through Grunwald's defense!

18:10.280 --> 18:13.820
And is reached by the South American black panther! What incredible speed!

18:13.820 --> 18:15.140
It's mine!

18:15.140 --> 18:16.740
Victorino shoots!

18:18.070 --> 18:19.300
The ball's cleared!

18:19.300 --> 18:20.480
It's no good!

18:20.480 --> 18:23.210
Our attack isn't over yet!

18:24.450 --> 18:26.380
Schester forcefully takes the ball!

18:26.380 --> 18:27.580
Margas appears!

18:30.580 --> 18:31.860
What?

18:33.850 --> 18:36.020
Their attack is fierce, just as expected.

18:39.730 --> 18:43.340
It's the opening game. I'll be sure to show 'em what I've got!

18:45.340 --> 18:50.240
It's a counter! Roland's not returned to their posts! This is their chance!

18:52.520 --> 18:56.140
I'll make up for my absence last season when I was injured.

18:56.140 --> 18:59.600
As long as the "Super Great Goalkeeper" is around,

18:59.600 --> 19:04.220
they'll see that the goalkeeper is the eleventh player on the field!

19:06.510 --> 19:10.590
It's in! FC Grunwald opens the score!

19:10.590 --> 19:13.240
They've succeeded in their counter!

19:13.240 --> 19:15.900
Is this the winning goal?

19:17.930 --> 19:19.980
We're already into stoppage time.

19:19.980 --> 19:23.220
Schester doesn't hide his eagerness to get the ball.

19:24.260 --> 19:27.340
He doesn't want to lose this home opening game!

19:28.660 --> 19:32.820
But it would not be a surprise if the referee blew the final whistle of this game at any moment now. {@sangofe: there, you got your long, awkward, literal-to-a-fault sentence, I hope you're happy}

19:35.570 --> 19:37.820
Roland tries one last attack.

19:38.620 --> 19:43.460
But their attacking players, Margas and Victorino, are being tightly marked.

19:43.460 --> 19:47.900
Is FC Grunwald just waiting for the final whistle?

19:49.700 --> 19:51.060
Damn it!

19:51.060 --> 19:53.740
Schester's out of passing options.

19:53.740 --> 19:56.300
Grunwald's whole team is playing defensively.

19:58.980 --> 20:03.500
Schester attempts to break through alone. Grunwald's defensive line backs up.

20:05.250 --> 20:07.820
I'll show you an aggressive defense!

20:12.540 --> 20:15.140
Despite being off balance, Schester prepares to shoot.

20:17.100 --> 20:20.140
Oh! Wakabayashi came out from the goal line and took the ball!

20:20.140 --> 20:22.510
Schester is falling to the ground!

20:26.010 --> 20:28.330
And with this, the game's over!

20:28.330 --> 20:29.910
It ends 1 - 0!

20:29.910 --> 20:35.380
FC Grunwald has magnificently won this opening away game!

20:38.020 --> 20:39.780
Yes!

21:01.650 --> 21:05.130
I see Tsubasa hasn't been sent to the substitutes' field yet.{note to sangofe: we're taking the "doing well" in the next line into consideration}

21:05.130 --> 21:11.010
Yeah, he's doing well in these tough practice games while playing on the substitute team.

21:11.010 --> 21:15.950
He might not get the starting position, but at least he'll be on the bench.

21:18.840 --> 21:19.540
Tsubasa.

21:19.540 --> 21:20.990
Yes!

21:20.990 --> 21:24.500
Play right midfielder on the regulars' team.

21:26.630 --> 21:28.690
Tsubasa's joining the regulars?

21:28.690 --> 21:30.540
As a right midfielder instead of a playmaker?!

21:35.510 --> 21:37.180
Tsubasa, here.

21:54.670 --> 21:56.950
Yes, I'll do my best!

22:04.020 --> 22:10.700
Preview

22:05.580 --> 22:07.940
We're doing a practice game here at FC Cataluña's training camp.

22:08.300 --> 22:11.940
I've been made the right midfielder on the regulars' team.

22:11.940 --> 22:15.000
I will run towards Rivaul-san's passes!

22:15.000 --> 22:18.580
I've already begun the fight to obtain a starting position!

22:19.220 --> 22:24.540
I heard Coach Edward asking me, "Which position do you want to play?"

22:24.540 --> 22:26.300
Next time, on Captain Tsubasa:

22:26.300 --> 22:27.820
A Harsh Notice

22:26.500 --> 22:34.220
A Harsh Notice

22:27.820 --> 22:29.540
Look forward to it!

22:29.540 --> 22:31.660
Let's face our future! Kick off!

